H1.definition:
a primitive word;
father, in a literal and immediate, or figurative and remote application
KJV: chief, (fore-) father(-less), [idiom] patrimony, principal. Compare names in 'Abi-'.

H3.definition:
from the same as H24 (אָבִיב);
a green plant
KJV: greenness, fruit.

H4.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3 (אֵב)
{a green plant}
KJV: fruit.

H5.definition:
of foreign origin;
Abagtha, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Abagtha.

H6.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to wander away, i.e. lose oneself; by implication to perish (causative, destroy)
KJV: break, destroy(-uction), [phrase] not escape, fail, lose, (cause to, make) perish, spend, [idiom] and surely, take, be undone, [idiom] utterly, be void of, have no way to flee.

H7.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6 (אָבַד)
{properly, to wander away, i.e. lose oneself; by implication to perish (causative, destroy)}
KJV: destroy, perish.

H8.definition:
active of participle of H6 (אָבַד);
(concrete) wretched or (abstract) destruction
KJV: perish.

H10.definition:
the same as H9 (אֲבֵדָה), miswritten for H11 (אֲבַדּוֹן);
a perishing
KJV: destruction.

H11.definition:
intensive from H6 (אָבַד);
abstract, a perishing; concrete, Hades
KJV: destruction.

H12.definition:
from H6 (אָבַד);
a perishing
KJV: destruction.

H13.definition:
from H6 (אָבַד);
a perishing
KJV: destruction.

H14.definition:
a primitive root;
to breathe after, i.e. (figuratively) to be acquiescent
KJV: consent, rest content will, be willing.

H16.definition:
from H14 (אָבָה) (in the sense of bending toward);
the papyrus
KJV: swift.

H17.definition:
from H14 (אָבָה) (in the sense of desiring);
want
KJV: sorrow.

H18.definition:
from H75 (אָבַס);
a manger or stall
KJV: crib.

H19.definition:
from an unused root (apparently meaning to turn);
brandishing of a sword
KJV: point.

H20.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a melon (only plural)
KJV: melon.

H21.definition:
from H1 (אָב); fatherly;
Abi, Hezekiah's mother
KJV: Abi.

H22.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H410 (אֵל); father (i.e. possessor) of God;
Abiel, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Abiel.

H23.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H622 (אָסַף); father of gathering (i.e. gatherer);
Abiasaph, an Israelite
KJV: Abiasaph.

H24.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to be tender);
green, i.e. a young ear of grain; hence, the name of the month Abib or Nisan
KJV: Abib, ear, green ears of corn (not maize).

H25.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H1391 (גִּבְעוֹן); father (i.e. founder) of Gibon;
Abi-Gibon, perhaps an Israelite
KJV: father of Gibeon.

H26.definition:
or shorter אֲבִיגַל; from H1 (אָב) and H1524 (גִּיל); father (i.e. source) of joy;
Abigail or Abigal, the name of two Israelitesses
KJV: Abigal.

H27.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H1777 (דִּין); father of judgment (i.e. judge);
Abidan, an Israelite
KJV: Abidan.

H28.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H3045 (יָדַע); father of knowledge (i.e. knowing);
Abida, a son of Abraham by Keturah
KJV: Abida, Abidah.

H29.definition:
or prolonged אֲבִיָּהוּ ; from H1 (אָב) and H3050 (יָהּ); father (i.e. worshipper) of Jah;
Abijah, the name of several Israelite men and two Israelitesses
KJV: Abiah, Abijah.

H30.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H1931 (הוּא); father (i.e. worshipper) of Him (i.e. God);
Abihu, a son of Aaron
KJV: Abihu.

H31.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H1935 (הוֹד); father (i.e. possessor) of renown;
Abihud, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Abihud.

H32.definition:
or (more correctly) אֲבִיחַיִל ; from H1 (אָב) and H2428 (חַיִל); father (i.e. possessor) of might;
Abihail or Abichail, the name of three Israelites and two Israelitesses
KJV: Abihail.

H33.definition:
from H44 (אֲבִיעֶזֶר) with the article inserted; father of the Ezrite;
an Abiezrite or descendant of Abiezer
KJV: Abiezrite.

H34.definition:
from H14 (אָבָה), in the sense of want (especially in feeling);
destitute
KJV: beggar, needy, poor (man).

H35.definition:
from H14 (אָבָה);
provocative of desire; the caper berry (from its stimulative taste)
KJV: desire.

H36.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H2898 (טוּב); father of goodness (i.e. good);
Abitub, an Israelite
KJV: Abitub.

H37.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H2919 (טַל); father of dew (i.e. fresh);
Abital, a wife of King David
KJV: Abital.

H38.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H3220 (יָם); father of (the) sea (i.e. seaman);
Abijam (or Abijah), a king of Judah
KJV: Abijam.

H39.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and an elsewhere unused (probably foreign) word; father of Mael (apparently some Arab tribe);
Abimael, a son of Joktan
KJV: Abimael.

H40.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H4428 (מֶלֶךְ); father of (the) king;
Abimelek, the name of two Philistine kings and of two Israelites
KJV: Abimelech.

H41.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H5068 (נָדַב); father of generosity (i.e. liberal);
Abinadab, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Abinadab.

H42.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H5278 (נֹעַם); father of pleasantness (i.e. gracious);
Abinoam, an Israelite
KJV: Abinoam.

H43.definition:
contracted from H23 (אֲבִיאָסָף);
Ebjasaph, an Israelite
KJV: Ebiasaph.

H44.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H5829 (עֵזֶר); father of help (i.e. helpful);
Abiezer, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Abiezer.

H45.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and an unused root of uncertain derivation; probably, father of strength (i.e. valiant);
Abialbon, an Israelite
KJV: Abialbon.

H46.definition:
from H82 (אָבַר);
mighty (spoken of God)
KJV: mighty (one).

H47.definition:
for H46 (אָבִיר)
{mighty (spoken of God)}
KJV: angel, bull, chiefest, mighty (one), stout(-hearted), strong (one), valiant.

H48.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H7311 (רוּם); father of height (i.e. lofty);
Abiram, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Abiram.

H49.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H7686 (שָׁגָה); father of error (i.e. blundering);
Abishag, a concubine of David
KJV: Abishag.

H50.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H7771 (שׁוֹעַ); father of plenty (i.e. prosperous);
Abishua, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Abishua.

H51.definition:
from H1 (אָב) and H7791 (שׁוּר); father of (the) wall (i.e. perhaps mason);
Abishur, an Israelite
KJV: Abishur.

H52.definition:
or (shorter) אַבְשַׁי ; from H1 (אָב) and H7862 (שַׁי); father of a gift (i.e. probably generous);
Abishai, an Israelite
KJV: Abishai.

H53.definition:
or (shortened) אַבְשָׁלוֹם ; from H1 (אָב) and H7965 (שָׁלוֹם); father of peace (i.e. friendly);
Abshalom, a son of David; also (the fuller form) a later Israelite
KJV: Abishalom, Absalom.

H54.definition:
contracted from H1 (אָב) and H3498 (יָתַר); father of abundance (i.e. liberal);
Ebjathar, an Israelite
KJV: Abiathar.

H55.definition:
a primitive root;
probably to coil upward
KJV: mount up.

H56.definition:
a primitive root;
to bewail
KJV: lament, mourn.

H58.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to be grassy);
a meadow
KJV: plain. Compare also the proper names beginning with Abel-.

H59.definition:
from H58 (אָבֵל); a meadow;
Abel, the name of two places in Palestine.
KJV: Abel.

H61.definition:
apparently from H56 (אָבַל) through the idea of negation;
nay, i.e. truly or yet
KJV: but, indeed, nevertheless, verily.

H62.definition:
from H58 (אָבֵל) and H1004 (בַּיִת) and H4601 (מַעֲכָה); meadow of Beth-Maakah;
Abel of Beth-maakah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Abel-beth-maachah, Abel of Beth-maachah,

H63.definition:
from H58 (אָבֵל) and the plural of H7848 (שִׁטָּה), with the article inserted; meadow of the acacias;
Abel hash-Shittim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Abelshittim.

H64.definition:
from H58 (אָבֵל) and the plural of H3754 (כֶּרֶם); meadow of vineyards;
Abel-Keramim, a place in Palestine
KJV: plain of the vineyards.

H65.definition:
from H58 (אָבֵל) and H4246 (מְחֹלָה)xlit mᵉchôwlâh corrected to mᵉchôlâh; meadow of dancing;
Abel-Mecholah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Abel-meholah.

H66.definition:
from H58 (אָבֵל) and H4325 (מַיִם); meadow of water;
Abel-Majim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Abel-maim.

H67.definition:
from H58 (אָבֵל) and H4714 (מִצְרַיִם); meadow of Egypt;
Abel-Mitsrajim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Abel-mizraim.

H68.definition:
from the root of H1129 (בָּנָה) through the meaning to build;
a stone
KJV: [phrase] carbuncle, [phrase] mason, [phrase] plummet, (chalk-, hail-, head-, sling-) stone(-ny), (divers) weight(-s).

H69.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H68 (אֶבֶן)
{a stone}
KJV: stone.

H70.definition:
from the same as H68 (אֶבֶן);
a pair of stones (only dual); a potter's wheel or a midwife's stool (consisting alike of two horizontal disks with a support between)
KJV: wheel, stool.

H72.definition:
from H68 (אֶבֶן) and H5828 (עֵזֶר) with the article inserted; stone of the help;
Eben-ha-Ezer, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ebenezer.

H73.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a belt
KJV: girdle.

H74.definition:
or (fully) אֲבִינֵר ; from H1 (אָב) and H5216 (נִיר); father of light (i.e. enlightening);
Abner, an Israelite
KJV: Abner.

H75.definition:
a primitive root;
to fodder
KJV: fatted, stalled.

H76.definition:
(by reduplication) from an unused root (meaning to belch forth);
an inflammatory pustule (as eruption)
KJV: blains.

H77.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to gleam; conspicuous;
Ebets, a place in Palestine
KJV: Abez.

H78.definition:
from the same as H76 (אֲבַעְבֻּעָה); splendid;
Ibtsan, an Israelite
KJV: Ibzan.

H79.definition:
a primitive root, probably to float away (as vapor), but used only as denominative from H80 (אָבָק);
to bedust, i.e. grapple
KJV: wrestle.

H80.definition:
from root of H79 (אָבַק);
light particles (as volatile)
KJV: (small) dust, powder.

H81.definition:
feminine of H80 (אָבָק)
{light particles (as volatile)}
KJV: powder.

H82.definition:
a primitive root;
to soar
KJV: fly.

H83.definition:
from H82 (אָבַר);
a pinion
KJV: (long-) wing(-ed).

H84.definition:
feminine of H83 (אֵבֶר)
{a pinion}
KJV: feather, wing.

H85.definition:
contracted from H1 (אָב) and an unused root (probably meaning to be populous); father of a multitude;
Abraham, the later name of Abram
KJV: Abraham.

H87.definition:
contracted from H48 (אֲבִירָם); high father;
Abram, the original name of Abraham
KJV: Abram.

H88.definition:
plural of H178 (אוֹב); water-skins;
Oboth, a place in the Desert
KJV: Oboth.

H89.definition:
of uncertain derivation (compare H90 (אֲגַג));
Age, an Israelite
KJV: Agee.

H90.definition:
or אֲגָג; of uncertain derivation (compare H89 (אָגֵא)); flame;
Agag, a title of Amalekitish kings
KJV: Agag.

H91.definition:
patrial or patronymic from H90 (אֲגַג);
an Agagite or descendent (subject) of Agag
KJV: Agagite.

H92.definition:
feminine passive participle of an unused root (meaning to bind);
a band, bundle, knot, or arch
KJV: bunch, burden, troop.

H93.definition:
prob of Persian origin;
a nut
KJV: nut.

H94.definition:
passive participle of H103 (אָגַר); gathered (i.e. received among the sages);
Agur, a fanciful name for Solomon
KJV: Agur.

H95.definition:
from the same as H94 (אָגוּר);
properly, something gathered, i.e. perhaps a grain or berry; used only of a small (silver) coin
KJV: piece (of) silver.

H96.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to flow down or together as drops);
a reservoir
KJV: drop.

H97.definition:
dual of H96 (אֶגֶל).; a double pond;
Eglajim, a place in Moab
KJV: Eglaim.

H98.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to collect as water);
a marsh; hence a rush (as growing in swamps); hence a stockade of reeds
KJV: pond, pool, standing (water).

H99.definition:
probably from the same as H98 (אֲגַם) (in the sense of stagnant water);
figuratively, sad
KJV: pond.
